            <section id="work" class="entries">
                <h3>Recent Work</h3>

                <p class="section-intro"><span class="company-label">Mod Op, 2024&ndash;2026.</span> I was a founding member of Mod Op's Innovation team and led a team of six as VP, Creative Innovation, in the company's first product engineering group. Mod Op is a roughly 500-person agency and formed its Innovation team with a $10M pledge to build out its AI practice. I helped design and build the Orion platform, its AI technology and tool stack, and owned six products in its portfolio, from concept through go-to-market, delivery, and refinement.</p>

                <p class="platform-feature">
                    <span class="feature-label">PLATFORM CASE STUDY</span>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus">Orion and Nexus: the AI operating layer</a></strong>
                    I led product vision and delivery for Nexus, the identity and knowledge service underneath Orion. It served common company data, client and project knowledge, user-managed agents that made that knowledge accessible and automation possible, and a chat harness that put those capabilities in everyone's hands securely.
                    <br />
                    <span class="fun-fact"><strong>95% employee adoption · 700+ agents deployed</strong> as of August 2026<br /><a href="https://digiday.com/marketing/build-or-buy-inside-indie-agency-mod-ops-ai-infrastructure/" target="_blank">Digiday put Orion's avoided licensing costs at roughly $3M</a> that same month.</span>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/nexus#cs-context">Brand Agents</a></strong> AI assistants grounded in a client's approved knowledge, voice, and goals, in use across agency and client work since April 2025. I helped shape the product and <a href="https://www.modop.com/blog/brand-agent-how-we-created-ai-that-actually-helps-clients/" target="_blank">wrote its launch story</a>. More than 200 client-specific Brand Agents were deployed by August 2026.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/geo">GEO by Mod Op</a></strong> Brand visibility monitoring across the major AI platforms. It went into internal use in June 2026 and <a href="https://www.modop.com/press/mod-op-launches-free-ai-search-visibility-tool-and-unveils-the-geo-50/" target="_blank">launched publicly</a> in August 2026 &ndash; the free version is <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">live now</a>. I took the concept from idea through prototype into production, working with the agency's search and strategy experts to turn weekslong manual audits into an automated free audit and a paid program for clients that want to take real steps to improve their visibility.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/launchpad">Launchpad</a></strong> A rapid prototyping platform with access control, self-serve deployment, and feedback built in. I built the first version and shipped it the morning our February 2026 hackathon began, so engineers could deploy six prototypes a day without waiting on DevOps. Two sprints across Innovation and Technology produced 60+ working prototypes, and Launchpad became a transparent internal showcase of Mod Op's AI roadmap.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong><a class="case-study-link" href="/mod-heat">Mod Heat</a></strong> Brand-aware news and trend tracking, ranked by relevance, risk, and reach. I originated the concept, pitched it to the executive team, and shipped it with my team as Mod Op Innovation&rsquo;s first product launch in November 2024.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <strong>Audience Lab</strong> Digital-twin audience simulation, grounded in real customer and buyer data, for creative pretesting and strategy.
